On Dec 1, 9:03 pm, Qwaszx86 <qwasz...@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm playing the best character of my Nethack career, and I haven't
> even gotten below lv 22 yet. While I've gotten farther before, I've
> never felt this well prepared, and I really don't want to blow it now
> with stupid decisions. A blessed ?oID just revealed to me that Ive
> been carrying a wand of wishing (0:3) for quite a while, and I want to
> know what I should be wishing for based on where I am.
>
> Here we go:
>
> Auren the Warrior
> AC:-11
> Exp: 15
>
> The only notable piece of armor I'm wearing is +5 GDSM.
> The rest of my armor is mildly enchanted (or not) elven leather helm,
> boots, cloak, gloves.
>
> I have reflection via the "oR.
>
> I am currently twoweaponing Greyswandir and another silver saber, but
> I have Moj tucked away in my bag of holding and I was also granted
> Ogresmasher from my god (left that upstairs)

Leave moj and ogresmasher tucked away, you have Greyswandir which the
best weapon in the game.  Silver sabre is fine as the off-hand weapon
(katanas are good too)

> I am expert in daggers, skilled in Longsword and Hammer, basic in
> Saber, and skilled in twoweapon combat.

Do _not_ waste any more slots on longsword/hammer (in general, expert
in melee weapons isn't worth it; especially for you since saber is how
you're going to want to go)

> I completed the quest and found the bell and the orb.
>
> I found Ludios, but haven't ventured there because I don't have
> =oconflict.
>
> I don't currently have a pet

Not worth a wish for a pet.

> I have the luckstone.
>
> So basically I was thinking of wishing for a magic marker so I could
> scribe some ?oEnchant Weapon, since none of my weapons are enchanted,
> but I'm also wondering if with three artifacts in the game I should
> risk wishing for fire/frost brand, since I can get expert in longsword
> presumably at some point.

No, they're both worse than Grayswandir even with lower skill in
saber.

> I also want better armor before I use the couple of ?oEA I have
> stashed away. What's worth it? Guantles of power? CoMR (don't think i
> really need it)? T-shirt (so i could enchant it)?

GoPower are largely useless by this point (earlier on they're very
valuable) for a valk, since you should be at or near max from the
quest.  If I'm planning on castng spells, I'd be ditching the GoPower
about now even if I'd found them laying around the dungeon w/o costing
a wish.  CoMR is unnecessary with GDSM.  Speed boots are nice, but
jumping are better if you're going to wish for something.

> I have holy water and at least one scroll of charging, so I'll
> definitely use that for as many wishes as possible, just need to know
> what I should get.

At least 2 markers, maybe 3; enchant up a full set of armor.  That's
GDSM, some gloves (leather is fine, dex if you have them), jumping
boots (wish for them if you've not found them), a helmet (brilliance
or telepathy if you have it, otherwise elvish leather), and a cloak
(robe if you're going to cast--kill a priest for it--or elvish or
whatever MC3 cloak).

Conflict would maybe merit a wish, as would teleport control if you
lack it.  Otherwise I'd keep a spare wish around for emergencies.

With MR and reflection and the best weapon around already in hand,
it's really getting AC down and not YASDing that you want to avoid.

As a first-timer, a "oLifeSaving would be quite nice but you'd need to
go SDSM + CoMR for that so maybe play with care until the castle and
switch there.


